          "why": "The arrangement accounts for all 20 electrons in a neutral calcium atom.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Calcium has 20 electrons.\nStep 2: Place 2 in the first shell. Remaining: 18.\nStep 3: Place 8 in the second shell. Remaining: 10.\nStep 4: Place 8 in the third shell. Remaining: 2.\nStep 5: Place the final 2 in the fourth shell.\nStep 6: Check: 2 + 8 + 8 + 2 = 20.",
          "hint": "Distribute 20 electrons across four occupied shells.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
