          "sol": "Step 1: Protons = 17.\nStep 2: Electrons = 18.\nStep 3: Charge = 17 − 18 = −1.\nStep 4: A chlorine ion with charge −1 is written Cl⁻.",
          "hint": "Subtract the number of electrons from the number of protons.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
          "chapter": "chemical_bonding",
