          "why": "The arrangement of charged ions explains the brittleness of ionic crystals.",
          "sol": "Step 1: The ionic crystal contains alternating positive and negative ions.\nStep 2: A force may shift the layers in the lattice.\nStep 3: The shift can place ions with the same charge next to each other.\nStep 4: Like charges repel, causing the crystal to split.",
