      "notes": "\n<h2>Ethanol</h2>\n\n<h3>1. What is ethanol?</h3>\n<p><strong>Ethanol</strong> is an alcohol containing two carbon atoms. The prefix <strong>eth-</strong> indicates two carbon atoms, while the ending <strong>-ol</strong> identifies the alcohol family.</p>\n\n<p>Its molecular formula is <strong>C₂H₆O</strong>. It is also commonly written as <strong>C₂H₅OH</strong>, which makes the hydroxyl group easier to recognise.</p>\n\n<h3>2. Understanding the formula</h3>\n<p>The condensed structural formula of ethanol is <strong>CH₃CH₂OH</strong>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CH₃ represents the first carbon group.</li>\n<li>CH₂ represents the second carbon group.</li>\n<li>OH is the hydroxyl functional group.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The two carbon atoms are joined by a single covalent bond. The atoms share electrons, and each carbon forms four covalent bonds in total.</p>\n\n<h3>3. Counting atoms</h3>\n<p>In C₂H₅OH, there are two carbon atoms, five hydrogen atoms in C₂H₅, one additional hydrogen in OH, and one oxygen atom. Therefore, the total is C₂H₆O.</p>\n\n<h3>Worked example 1: Convert the formula</h3>\n<p><strong>Question:</strong> Write the molecular formula of ethanol from C₂H₅OH.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Count carbon atoms: C₂ means 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Count hydrogen atoms: H₅ plus the H in OH gives 5 + 1 = 6.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Count oxygen atoms: there is 1 O.</p>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong> C₂H₆O.</p>\n\n<h3>Worked example 2: Calculate relative molecular mass</h3>\n<p><strong>Question:</strong> Calculate the relative molecular mass of ethanol, C₂H₆O. Use C = 12, H = 1 and O = 16.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Carbon contribution = 2 × 12 = 24.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Hydrogen contribution = 6 × 1 = 6.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Oxygen contribution = 1 × 16 = 16.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Add the contributions: 24 + 6 + 16 = 46.</p>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Relative molecular mass = 46.</p>\n\n<h3>Worked example 3: Find the percentage by mass of oxygen</h3>\n<p><strong>Question:</strong> Calculate the percentage by mass of oxygen in ethanol, C₂H₆O.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Relative molecular mass = 46.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Mass contributed by oxygen = 16.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Percentage of oxygen = (16 ÷ 46) × 100.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Percentage of oxygen ≈ 34.8%.</p>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Approximately 34.8% oxygen by mass.</p>\n",
