          "why": "The high-temperature flame is useful for cutting and welding metals.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Oxygen supports combustion.\nStep 2: A fuel burning in oxygen can produce a very hot flame.\nStep 3: The hot flame can melt or cut metals.",
          "hint": "Focus on the core principle of Uses of Oxygen.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
          "chapter": "air_water_environment",
          "topic": "Uses of Oxygen",
          "conceptId": "chemistry_air_water_environment_uses_of_oxygen",
