      "notes": "<h2>Hard Water</h2>\n\n  <p>Hard water contains dissolved calcium and magnesium ions.</p>\n\n  <p>These ions react with soap to form an insoluble substance called <strong>scum</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h3>Effects of hard water</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Soap does not lather easily.</li>\n    <li>Scum is formed.</li>\n    <li>More soap is required for washing.</li>\n    <li>Some types of hard water can form scale in pipes and boilers.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Important distinction</h3>\n  <p>Hard water is not necessarily unsafe to drink. The main problem considered here is its behaviour with soap and heating systems.</p>",
