      "notes": "<h2>Bauxite</h2>\n\n  <p><strong>Bauxite</strong> is the main ore from which aluminium is extracted.</p>\n\n  <p>It contains aluminium compounds together with impurities such as iron(III) oxide, silicon compounds and other materials.</p>\n\n  <p>Because aluminium is very reactive, it is not extracted from its ore by simple reduction with carbon.</p>\n\n  <h3>Extraction of Aluminium</h3>\n\n  <p>The extraction of aluminium involves:</p>\n\n  <ol>\n    <li>Obtaining bauxite.</li>\n    <li>Purifying the bauxite to obtain aluminium oxide.</li>\n    <li>Electrolysing molten aluminium oxide to produce aluminium.</li>\n  </ol>\n\n  <p>The purified aluminium oxide is commonly called <strong>alumina</strong>.</p>",
